# user_unit_stdlib_shadow.z -- a hidden subunit named for a stdlib unit. The
# member lookup took its frame root from the unit-name index, so `io.tag` was
# looked for in the STDLIB io, which has no `tag`. Reaching io's own members
# from a unit that does NOT shadow it must still work.
main: function is {
    print "shadowy.pick=\{shadowy.pick}"
    io.print "io still reachable"
}
